PHASE 3D — PRODUCTION MODEL VALIDATION, RETRAINING & DEPLOYMENT

We are now moving from Phase 3C.8 into Phase 3D.

Phase 3C.8 produced candidate v2 implementations for:

- Expected Minutes
- xG
- xA

The candidate models addressed:

1. Synthetic recent-start / low-sample minutes errors.
2. Current-club role evidence.
3. Sample-size-aware xG shrinkage.
4. Sample-size-aware xA shrinkage.
5. Recency + long-term ability separation.
6. Transfer-aware role handling.
7. Per-fixture DGW handling.

Phase 3C.8 demonstrated strong improvement on its 2025/26 out-of-sample evaluation.

However, the candidate models have NOT yet replaced production models.

Production currently remains:

- expected_minutes_v1
- xg_v1_lgbm
- xa_v1_lgbm
- existing statistical CS / DEFCON / Bonus components

The objective of Phase 3D is to determine whether the candidate methodology is robust enough to become production.

DO NOT modify the optimizer yet.

DO NOT tune the optimizer to produce a particular FPL squad.

DO NOT manually force Bruno Fernandes, João Pedro, Calvert-Lewin, Haaland or any other player into the team.

The model must earn those selections through its projections.

